# Job Number timeline

Owner-only typed Job Number retrieval. Not the forensic Granot lifecycle
projection (`projections.ts` / `GranotTimelineEntry`).

Service doc:
[`docs/knowledge/services/job-number-timeline.md`](../../docs/knowledge/services/job-number-timeline.md).

## Workspace

Enhancement work is the delivery pack
[`docs/job-number-timeline/README.md`](../../docs/job-number-timeline/README.md).
Start there → `AGENT-PROTOCOL.md` → `PROGRESS.md`. There is no
`ready` issue. Specification wins on additive behavior; the prototype
spec wins on event truth, correlation, and masking.

JTE-01 extract, JTE-02 v2 projection, JTE-03 evaluators, JTE-04
Admin UI, JTE-05 (live proof, deep links), and JTE-06 (cancellation
correlation snapshots) shipped. JTE-07 stays deferred. Admin
displays server arrays; it does not evaluate.

## Seams

- After JTE-01, **no file under `src/` imports**
  `scripts/prototypes/job-number-timeline`. The CLI may adapt over
  `src/services/jobNumberTimeline`.
- Route stays thin: authorize, validate, `module.read`, respond.
- Tests call the same module interface as the route. Mongo and memory
  loaders both exist, or the loader seam is fake.
- `projector.ts` calls `outcome.ts` (`evaluateCurrentOutcome`,
  `assessStages`, `outcomeHeadline`) and `attention.ts` (one evaluator
  per specification §8 attention and limitation code, `evaluateFreshness`)
  after events and activities are finalized. The external seam stays
  `createJobNumberTimelineModule({ loader }).read`.

## Invariants

- Read-time projection only. No `OperationalEvent`, no second event
  stream, no mutation, no notification.
- Intake is never the official outcome. `evaluateCurrentOutcome` uses
  specification §4.2 precedence, not last-event-wins. Latest Decision
  attempt only. Sheet Sync joins by entity ID, never Job Number.
- No inferred events. No Job Number catalog. No `$lookup` on the hot
  route. Cap 250 events with a named truncation limitation.
- Always emit `MULTI_QUERY_READ`, `MOVE_COMPLETION_UNAVAILABLE`, and
  `GOOGLE_DESTINATION_UNVERIFIED`. Keep `TIMELINE_TRUNCATED` when the
  250 cap hits. Do not invent extra §8 codes.
- Never leak contact, SMS body, transcript, recording, provider payload,
  Sheet ID, Sheet row, or raw error body.
- Admin must not recompute outcome, attention, or limitations. Golden
  pages in `golden-pages.ts` remain test fixtures. JTE-04 Admin UI
  displays those arrays; it does not evaluate them.
- WordPress Lead creation is not a source receipt
  (`WORDPRESS_RECEIPT_UNAVAILABLE`). Sheet `synced` is not Google
  equality. Delivery stays `unverifiable` even when every outbox job is
  synced. Move completion is a limitation, never a stage or event.
- RingCentral-born pages emit `RINGCENTRAL_CURSOR_BOUNDED` and fill
  `freshness.ringcentral_covered_through` plus
  `ringcentral_cursor_lag_seconds`. `google_destination_readback` stays
  `not_performed`. `consistency` stays `multi_query_best_effort`.
- `SHEET_SYNC_PENDING_TOO_LONG_MS` default is 1 hour (module constant,
  not `process.env`).
- After JTE-06, the Mongo loader hops `cancelled_leads` by indexed
  `normalized_job_no_snapshot` when present (`equivalentNormalizedJobSnapshotFilter`),
  merged with booking-linked rows. Assemble still refuses orphans
  without a durable job snapshot.

## Residuals

- JTE-01: CLI company/granularity mismatch prints `filtered_out`
  (exit 0).
- JTE-02: the module stamps `assembled_at` with
  `input.now ?? new Date()`. RingCentral `source_received` is qualified
